---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Sopsdeck — a visual browser and editor for your secrets"
  description="A visual browser and editor for your secrets. Manage SOPS-encrypted dotenv, JSON, and YAML files locally, on your own or with a team."
  active="product"
>
  <section class="hero hero--landing">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="kicker">For individual developers and teams</div>
      <h1>A visual browser and editor for your secrets.</h1>
      <p>
        A simple, flexible way to manage SOPS-encrypted dotenv, JSON, and YAML files. Edit locally,
        share access with your team, and track changes in Git.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="#start">Install with npm</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="#product">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-still">
      <img
        src="/assets/editor.png"
        width="1440"
        height="900"
        alt="Sopsdeck showing a production secrets file with values hidden"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" id="product">
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">SOPS</div>
      <h2>Keep secrets in your project</h2>
      <p>
        Work with dotenv, JSON, and YAML files encrypted with SOPS. Your local files are the source
        of truth. Publish selected secrets to GitHub Actions when you need them.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">Access</div>
      <h2>Share access with your team</h2>
      <p>
        Add a teammate’s Age public key to grant access to a file. Each person decrypts it with
        their own private key.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">Git</div>
      <h2>Review and track changes</h2>
      <p>
        Review edits before committing, browse secret history, and sync encrypted files through Git.
        If branches diverge, Sopsdeck stops so you can resolve them.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="split" id="trust">
    <div>
      <div class="kicker">Editor</div>
      <h2>All your projects in one editor</h2>
      <p>
        Open a project folder, choose a file, and edit its secrets. Values stay hidden until you
        reveal them, and saving encrypts your changes on disk.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="product-still">
      <img
        src="/assets/editor.png"
        width="1440"
        height="900"
        alt="Project folders, a secrets editor, and access settings in Sopsdeck"
      />
      <figcaption>Browse files, edit values, and manage access from the same view.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="start" id="start">
    <div class="kicker">Install · macOS, Windows, and Linux</div>
    <h2>Open Sopsdeck in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Install with npm, then open a project folder. SOPS is included; all you need is Node.js and
      Git.
    </p>
    <pre>npm install -D sopsdeck
npx sopsdeck .

# global shortcut
npm install -g sopsdeck
sd .</pre>
    <p>The npm package downloads the matching local runner on first launch.</p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
